# NOTICE

**English**

This file records the third-party sources and attribution statements of OMZ (Oh My ZCode). `LICENSE`
contains only the full MIT text of this project itself, so that GitHub's license detection correctly
identifies it as MIT; the source statements are collected here.

## Upstream source: oh-my-openagent (OmO)

OMZ's orchestration protocol — the ultrawork lifecycle, plus the protocol text of the four skills
`ulw-plan` / `ulw-execute` / `ulw-research` / `review-work` — is **selectively ported** from
oh-my-openagent (OmO), repository <https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent>. The port is
capability parity and a rewrite, not a whole-repository fork and not code transplantation; the sync
discipline is in `DESIGN.md` §16.

- Per-path source pinning (`source` / `ported_paths` / `omz_target` / `port_status`) is in
  `upstream/omo-sources.lock.json`.
- Upstream license information, the sync process, and the non-applicable paths are in the `license`
  block of `upstream/omo-sources.lock.json` and in `upstream/README.md`. Those two places are
  authoritative; this file does not restate any license conclusion.
- The evidence status can be inspected on the spot with `node tools/doctor.mjs --supply-chain` (the
  `supply:lock` and `supply:upstream-license` items).

## Optional external dependency

The `graph` profile requires the user to install `@colbymchenry/codegraph` themselves; this
repository contains neither its code nor its index, and makes no statement about its license.
Installation and version evidence are likewise available via `node tools/doctor.mjs --supply-chain`.

